Review complete. Findings written to `docs/reviews/equipment-wh/equip-wh-02-draw-tempering-model.md`.

**Summary**: 4 findings — 1 critical, 1 high, 1 medium, 1 low.

| Severity | Finding |
|----------|---------|
| **Critical** | Unmet load computed from post-heating outlet temp instead of pre-heating snapshot; same-step element heat inflates `outlet_temp_c` and under-reports `unmet_load_w` |
| **High** | Hot-draw TMV gate keys off `setpoint > hot_draw` (HARES) vs `setpoint > tempered_draw` (OCHRE); in standard config HARES never tempers hot draws even when tank is overheated |
| **Medium** | `DrawResult.outlet_temp_c` doc claims "beginning of draw" but `apply_draw` computes it from post-injection temps; energy accounting correctly uses pre-injection snapshot — inconsistency across the struct |
| **Low** | Denominator `.max(1e-9)` guard in TMV vol_ratio is harmless but correctly unreachable under normal conditions |
